===Noun===
{{en-noun|~}}

# The act of taking something up, by [[tightening]], [[absorption]], or [[reeling]] in.
# {{lb|en|machinery}} That which takes up or [[tighten]]s; specifically, a device in a [[sewing]] [[machine]] or [[loom]] for drawing up the [[slack]] thread as the [[needle]] rises, in completing a [[stitch]].
# [[acceptance|Acceptance]] (of a proposal, offer, request, etc.).
#: {{ux|en|the '''take-up''' of benefits by the unemployed}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|date=2023 July 26|author=Jim Steer|title=Where rail can win modal shift|journal=RAIL|issue=988|page=40|text=As a first step, Mode Shift Revenue Support (MSRS) funding should be expanded, to ensure a higher '''take-up''' of unused freight paths in today's timetable and to help shape a sustainable path for multi-modal UK logistics.}}

